 "seconds": 14.3,
 "text": "1. **A** — 101110 in binary is 32 + 8 + 4 + 2 = 46.\n2. **C** — Brahmadesh (Burma) is now called Myanmar.\n3. **D** — The density of air at STP is about 1.293 kg m⁻³.\n4. **C** — Parabens act as endocrine disruptors, and this is linked to early puberty in girls.\n5. **A** — The period is T = 2π√(m/k), so it scales with √m. Making the mass 4m doubles the period to 2T.\n6. **C** — Bharatchandra Ray Gunakar died in 1760.\n7. **A** — 'Lalsalu' was written in 1948.\n8. **D** — 68 people received the Bir Uttom title.\n9. **A** — Write the numbers as 7k and 8k. Their LCM is 56k = 280, so k = 5, which is the HCF.\n10. **B** — (a − x)²⁰ has 21 terms, so the middle term is the 11th.\n11. **A** — The Adam's apple is on the larynx (voice box).\n12. **A** — The functional group of aldehydes is –CHO.\n13. **B** — Bangladeshi exam keys attribute this quote to Ivor Jennings; I'm answering from recall of those keys, not a confirmed source.\n14. **D** — Durba grass is *Cynodon dactylon*.\n15. **B** — The line 4x + 3y − 30 = 0 passes through (3, 6), since 12 + 18 − 30 = 0. Its distance from the origin is 30/5 = 6.\n\n{\"answers\": {\"5180e158-98d6-404f-8650-02f3ede675f6-141782\": \"A\", \"51e41a2d-4394-4383-94cc-5cbc8b388046-40205\": \"C\", \"526fe4b4-110c-421c-97de-2ee962d29f6c-22915\": \"D\", \"5368ce50-9f63-4a29-b5e8-a9fc6b92e12a-138704\": \"C\", \"559babbb-1a53-4c7c-8149-72be468bab7a-89256\": \"A\", \"57cec89d-1a5e-46eb-9a9c-d1c9fa08c184-71498\": \"C\", \"57ec3871-00ef-465b-b04d-b7549b9e1ff5-82040\": \"A\", \"5877834c-b7a2-479e-96e2-cd6605538cf9-14494\": \"D\", \"5bd76b77-9209-4602-8460-29b6d46f1387-94903\": \"A\", \"5e0700ef-d7f3-4d83-b6a4-c133828d34db-47550\": \"B\", \"61c9c0a1-731b-49ea-a7c3-d80138bb13af-121214\": \"A\", \"63b81d6c-0a00-43ac-8f4b-0c376d778a91-59057\": \"A\", \"64d3b462-8719-429a-9405-95bee8a76cbd-15523\": \"B\", \"64fa9f46-e87a-45e1-bd09-2ddf29cac193-84922\": \"D\", \"658d8db2-8adf-4607-9086-1c98fdc53143-36213\": \"B\"}}",
